{:edb/db-before-t 1122 :edb/db-after-t 1123 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534435 50 #inst "2026-10-11T20:43:38.738Z" 13194139534435 17592186045417 true] [17592186122684 1078 #edb/ref 17592186122687 13194139534435 17592186045417 true] [17592186124476 1038 #edb/ref 17592186421492 13194139534435 17592186045417 true] [17592186125014 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534435 17592186045417 true] [17592186125014 1071 "The level curves of the function $f(x, y) = x^{3}y - y^{2}x$ are given by $f(x, y) = c$. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $c =-1$ gives a line\n2. $c = 0$ gives a parabola and the axes $x = 0$ and $y = 0$\n3. $c = 1$ gives two lines" 13194139534435 17592186045417 false] [17592186125014 1071 "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{3}y-{y}^{2}x$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $c=-1$ gives a line\n\nII. $c=0$ gives a parabola and the axes $x=0$ and $y=0$\n\nIII. $c=1$ gives two lines" 13194139534435 17592186045417 true] [17592186125014 1074 "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}y-{y}^{2}x & =c \\\\ xy({x}^{2}-y) & =c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=\\pm 1$ then the level curves are $xy({x}^{2}-y)=\\pm 1,$ which are not lines.\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curves are $xy({x}^{2}-y)=0,$ which consists of the axes $x=0$ and $y=0$, and the parabola $y={x}^{2}.$\n\nSo, only statement II is true." 13194139534435 17592186045417 true] [17592186338937 1071 "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $c=1$ gives a line\n- $c=2$ gives a hyperbola\n- $c=0$ gives two lines" 13194139534435 17592186045417 false] [17592186338937 1071 "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $c=1$ gives a line\n\nII. $c=2$ gives a hyperbola\n\nIII. $c=0$ gives two lines" 13194139534435 17592186045417 true] [